Mad Libs Game in C

This is a simple Mad Libs Game developed using the C programming language.
The program asks the user to enter different words, such as adjectives, nouns, and verbs.
It then uses these words to generate a funny and creative story.

Concepts Learned

Through this project, I practised the following C programming concepts:

Variables: Declaring and storing data using character arrays.
Strings: Understanding strings and character arrays in C.
fgets(): Taking string input from the user.
sizeof(): Finding the size of an array.
strlen(): Finding the length of a string.
String manipulation: Removing the newline character using \0.
Header files: Using stdio.h and string.h.
Basic program structure: Understanding the main() function and return 0.

How the Game Works

The program asks the user to enter an adjective.
It asks for a noun.
It asks for another adjective.
It asks for a verb ending in -ing.
It asks for one more adjective.
Finally, it generates a funny story using the entered words.

What I Learned

This project helped me understand how to take user input, store strings in character arrays, manipulate strings, and display dynamic output using C.